Z||000001||FieroFanaticus2||11-05-2001||07:39 PM||||Crate them.  How much would it be for UPS?  $70 seems about right, but I'd check around, you might be able to get it a little less.<BR>For those who don't know, doors are A LOT heavier than what they look!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Swany||11-05-2001||07:51 PM||||I would look into using a freight company, such as viking freight, or pilot air frieght.<P>I used to be a commercial airliner parts broker, and I used to have to ship very large, and heavy parts alot. And rates for fed ex and ups for items of that size and weight are insane.. <P>Freight may take a little longer, although I don't think it is any slower than ups ground, but you will save a ton of money.||||reg||1
